HST Office: switching document tabs no longer flashes the desktop (all modules, mostly visible on Windows).

A tab switch shows the window of the new tab and hides the window of the old one. vcl paints a newly shown
window later (the frame's paint idle) and Skia copies the picture to the screen later still, so for about one
screen refresh after the old window was hidden there was no picture at all and the desktop behind showed
through: the screen flashed on every switch (error report HSTO-000006, HST Sheets on Windows; measured on
Windows 11 for HST Writer, Sheets, Slides, Draw and PDF alike).
The tab group now paints the shown window and flushes it to the screen (Window::PaintImmediately, then
OutputDevice::Flush) at once, and hides the previous tab only from an idle of the lowest priority, after
vcl has done its layout, painting and flush to the screen, painting and flushing the shown tab once more
first: on a switch (tab click, Ctrl+Alt+. / Ctrl+Alt+,) and when a document was opened. When a tab dropped on
another window's strip replaces its shown tab, and when the shown tab is closed and its neighbour takes
over, the shown window is painted and flushed before the previous one goes. Until it is hidden, the previous
tab stays under the shown one with the same position and size, so nothing changes on the screen.
License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_document_tab_switch_no_flash.py; on Windows tests/runtime/check-windows-tab-switch-flash.py
(measured: before 9 of 10 module runs flashed, 56-73% of the screen desktop; first version of this fix 1 of 10).
